Z||000005||86SE||08-16-2001||12:28 AM||||My 2.8 auto has the same idle problem you are talking about.  It will idle fine at 1000 after driving then it will jump up to about 1300, and fall to about 500, then jump to 1300 and fall to 500.  If i just give it a tap on the throttle it will idle normal for 10 seconds, then it will start back over again.  My problem isnt consistant.  It went away for about 5000 miles, now its back again. Hmmmm...i'll check my muffler bearings.<P>Chuck<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg">   <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>V-6 w/rod knock Yellow Fiero<BR> -- 3.4L Conversion *Back in session!* --||||reg||1
