Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||08-16-2001||08:15 PM||||That's not what I meant by how do your plugs look. What I meant was how do they look as far as coloration? If they're very white looking around the electrode this is a sign of running lean. If the colors brownish that's right where you want to be. If it's very dark or black that's not good.<P>If the color shows a lean condition then an <BR>adjustable fuel pressure regulator can help by feeding some more fuel to your hungry engine. When you mod. an engine it sometimes needs more fuel to compensate for the increased power. If you have a stock engine and your idles off then this is something else.<P>BTW sorry for the confusion with the plugs I<BR>should have been more clear.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000009||Patrick86GT||08-16-2001||11:44 PM||||Like my children, I have 4 2.8's and every damn one of them idles differently (yet, I love them equally).  Some with the odd stuff you guys mention, and some perfectly steady, new parts notwithstanding.  <P>I am becoming convinced that while all my children have the same father, it's the 4 different mothers that have made the difference.  Perhaps there can be no consistancy! <P>Any thoughts?||||reg||1
